comments.text:
Round-7 wiring (2026-10-29, SwiftBasin). The M0 e2e now also waits on: the Mine Stats reader (GATE-BULL-01 parts 1 and 3 are measured over Mine Stats values), BD-329 (zero uncited numbers), BD-331 (part 2, five-state ledger complete), BD-338 (live-dependency proof), BD-339 (reproduction kit and CI job) and the GATE-BULL-01 part-3 bead.
Logging contract the e2e must meet (so a failure is diagnosable from the log alone), one NDJSON line per event through bd-142's harness:
- per registered file: file, kind, sha256, bytes, tables_located, cells_read by kind, refusals, digest;
- per identity instance: family, table locator, operands with locators, state (i..v, np), certificate digest for (iii), missing fact for (iv), refusal code for (v);
- per vintage comparison (part 3): series key, first-publication value, later value, rounding_only flag, state;
- per run: lane (real or synthetic), gate_eligible, counts per state, uncited count (must be 0), state root, anchor, wall-clock, git sha.
The run must execute twice and assert byte-identical output (GATE-BULL-01 rerun clause) and must refuse (exit 8) when any registered file is missing or altered.

BD-078 done-when "Exhaust tests", at commit 8d88c0f (fmine-runtime/src/budget.rs, budget/tests.rs, CONTRACT.md).

What exists: Budget{deadline_ns, poll_quota, cost_quota, priority} with meet (tighter limit, higher priority; UNLIMITED is the identity); budget_table(&Params) -> the five §26.7 rows; OnExhaust{RefuseBatch, SealEarly, Cancel, Drain, Reconcile} with exit_code 6 / 9 / none; Meter on caller-supplied virtual time that refuses (never clamps) and stays exhausted; BudgetRow::meter(parent, now) meets the row with its parent's budget.

Exhaust tests (one per row, last allowed step checked one ns or one unit before each limit):
- ledger writer: refused at 250 ms, exit 6, sticky afterwards;
- telemetry: seals early past 64 MiB (refused bytes not recorded) and at 1 s;
- estimation run: cancels past blocks x realizations, and at the parent's 1 h deadline when nested under it (4 h alone);
- peer session: drains at window bytes / window end; the next window's meter starts fresh;
- finance bridge: indeterminate at 120 s (debug fa) / 10 s, exit 9.
Oracle: the_table_is_the_plans_table parses the plan's §26.7 table (deadline, cost, priority, action, "(exit 6)") and §30.1's exit-code table (Indeterminate = 9).
Planted bugs (all four together, reverted): deadline `>` instead of `>=`, cost `>=` instead of `>`, meet keeping the lower priority, telemetry priority 181. 8 of 10 budget tests failed; each plant hit at least one.

Fresh re-run after the revert, tree identical to 8d88c0f: cargo test -p fmine-runtime 25 + 1 + 4 passed; clippy -p fmine-runtime --all-targets -D warnings clean (remote vmi1227854); rustfmt --check clean; xtask check-all exit 0; ubs budget.rs 0 warnings.

Not independently verified: solo work; no second agent reviewed it. Choices the plan does not state: priority under meet takes the higher; no row has a poll quota; a meter reports the action but nothing yet carries it out (no region runs). CI has not run on 8d88c0f (not pushed).

bd-145 evidence (SwiftBasin).

commit: 37d4fe9 "fmine-numerics: lift fs-sparse CSR, LDLt + AMD and PCG (bd-145)". Local only: not pushed, so CI has not run it.

test: fresh clone checked out at 37d4fe9, `cargo test -p fmine-numerics sparse`: 34 passed, 0 failed. The done-when ("Residual known answers") is the three guard tests named in registries/lifts.toml:
- sparse::direct::tests::test_ldlt_residual_known_answers. Closed forms, not outputs of the code: tridiag(-1,2,-1)·x = 1 gives x_i = i(51−i)/2, and ·x = e₁ gives x_i = (51−i)/51, under both Natural and AMD orderings. [[0,1],[1,0]]·x = (3,5) gives (5,3) through a 2×2 pivot. KKT [[2I₃,Bᵀ],[B,0]]·x = (6,9,6,1,2) gives (1,2,3,4,5). The 16×16 grid Laplacian has an integer manufactured solution.
- sparse::precond::tests::test_pcg_residual_known_answers. The T_50 parabola is checked with an a priori error bound (κ ≤ 2601 from sin t ≥ 2t/π). ILU(0) of a tridiagonal matrix is the exact LU, so PCG takes 1 iteration. The grid manufactured solution uses κ ≤ 289, and ILU(0) takes fewer iterations than plain CG.
- sparse::tests::test_spmv_matches_dense_reference.

test: shared tree before the commit (the same bytes):
- `cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast`: 889 passed, 0 failed, 42 ignored, 64 suites;
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean;
- `cargo fmt --all --check`: clean;
- `cargo run -p xtask -- check-all`: exit 0, with only the warnings that were there before (proposed refusal codes, fmine-public BUDGET-AMEND-001).

ubs on the five changed .rs files: 0 critical. The three sparse files have no unwrap, expect or panic above `#[cfg(test)]`.

test: 14 mutants planted in a scratch clone, never in the shared tree. Each was killed by named tests, and every restore was checked by sha256:
- direct.rs:
  - 2×2 inertia sign;
  - zero-pivot floor dropped;
  - delayed pivots disabled;
  - solve length check removed;
  - 1×1 inertia sign;
  - AMD degree update removed (caught by the grid fill test).
- precond.rs:
  - pᵀAp breakdown check;
  - ILU pivot check;
  - ILU back-substitution diagonal;
  - rᵀz breakdown check.
- sparse.rs:
  - from_parts monotone check;
  - from_parts past-nnz check;
  - COO duplicate accumulation;
  - SpMV accumulation.

Differentials: LDLᵀ against crate::cholesky_solve (dense, no shared code) on random diagonally dominant SPD matrices, and PCG + ILU(0) against LDLᵀ.

Scope: as the bead title says, CSR/COO with SpMV, AMD with supernodal LDLᵀ and Sylvester inertia, and PCG with ILU(0). Upstream panics became typed refusals: SparseError, LdltError (with Invariant replacing asserts), IluError and PcgError. PcgError never carries an iterate. Left out, as each file's first line says: BSR, SELL-C-σ, the x86 FMA capsule, ops (transpose, SpGEMM), nested dissection, Chebyshev and SA-AMG. Plan §27.1 wave 0 lists SA-AMG under fs-sparse; it is not lifted here because it needs ops.

Known flag: `xtask check-lifts --upstream` (local only, never in CI) reads precond.rs at 15%, under MIN_OVERLAP_PERCENT 20, and so flags it "not_a_lift". The cause is that upstream keeps its PCG/ILU tests in tests/precond_battery.rs, so this file's 120 distinct test lines can share nothing with src/precond.rs. The code above `#[cfg(test)]` shares 29% (38 of 129 lines). sparse.rs measures 35% and direct.rs 78%. lifts.toml says this in a comment on the row.

Gate-test change, needing an independent reviewer: crates/xtask/src/lifts.rs.
- test_committed_registry_passes_with_four_lifts_and_five_analogues is renamed ..._seven_lifts_... and now asserts (7, 5).
- The local test test_upstream_known_answers_when_a_checkout_is_given now expects Err and asserts:
  - 7 rows;
  - every sha256_ok true;
  - exactly one flagged row, precond.rs with shared 38;
  - the old det/philox/color known answers.
- Control: a corrupted direct.rs digest in a scratch clone fails it.

Not independently verified:
- All of the above is my own re-execution. No other agent or person has reviewed the diff.
- CI has not run 37d4fe9.
- No cross-host determinism check: the files are DeterministicPerIsa, and only single-host bitwise repeats are tested.
- Nothing calls sparse yet. bd-149 (WLS), bd-238 (kriging) and bd-251 (PDLP) are open.

Template and checker: commit:96688ca (local main, not pushed).

What landed:
- docs/templates/CONTRACT.md has the twelve headings in order (1 Purpose ... 12 Proof obligations), each with one guidance line from the parent Design. Section 1 carries Crate, Layer, Subsystem, LOC budget and Allowed Module Families. The subsystem placeholder names all eighteen §0.5 subsystems; Lodestar was missing.
- crates/xtask/src/contracts.rs `check_contract_text(crate, contract, budget, refusal_codes) -> (errors, warnings)`; `findings` gives the same results by rule. It fails a contract when:
  - its level-2 headings are not exactly `## <n>. <Name>` for the twelve, once each, in order, with no other level-2 heading (lines in fenced code are not headings);
  - a section is empty;
  - section 1's `Layer`, `Subsystem` or `LOC budget` line differs from the registry row (written `26,000 planned / 30,000 ceiling`);
  - the subsystem is not one of the eighteen;
  - a crate other than xtask has no row.
  xtask's line must read `LOC budget: not budgeted (dev-only tool; no row in registries/loc_budget.toml)`. An `FMINE-REF-nnn` that is not in registries/refusals.toml is a warning, because BD-328 (bd-h0q1) is still open.
- `cargo run -p xtask -- contracts` prints one `{"crate","headings_ok","budget_ok","layer_ok","subsystem_ok","unregistered_codes"}` line per crates/*/CONTRACT.md, then `{"contracts","errors","warnings"}`, and exits 2 on any error.
- `contracts --write-budget` rewrites only those three lines. It matches the key in any case, so it finds the old `LOC Budget` lines, and it keeps line endings. When a section 1 lacks exactly one of each line, it refuses the whole run and writes nothing.
- CrateBudgetRow gained `subsystem`, which check_loc_budget now reads. check_all and check_scope are unchanged, as this bead requires; S2 switches check_all.

Deviations from the bead text:
- The tests live in crates/xtask/src/contracts.rs `mod tests`, not lib.rs `mod tests`, following the oracle, lifts and refusals modules. The names are the specified ones.
- The new `xtask contracts` command prints the per-crate line, not `check-scope`. S2 can call `contracts::findings` from check_scope when it wires the checker in.
- `--write-budget` writes plain values (`- **Layer:** U`). It drops the old backticks and layer glosses such as "(User Surfaces & CLI)".

Evidence. Everything below was re-run in a fresh clone at 96688ca with a fresh target directory.
- Tests:
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_misnamed_heading_fails
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_heading_out_of_order_fails
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_empty_section_fails
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_missing_validity_domain_fails (parent criterion 4)
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_budget_mismatch_fails (fmine-cli 14k/16k against 26,000/30,000; parent criterion 4)
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_subsystem_not_in_section_0_5_fails
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_unregistered_refusal_warns
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_contract_xtask_unbudgeted_line_accepted
  - test:xtask::contracts::tests::test_write_budget_is_idempotent
  - also test_template_form_passes, test_thousands_separators and test_subsystems_are_the_registry_set (the constant equals the registry's set).
- Mutation. The bead's own mutant, the heading rule reverted to the number prefix `## <n>. `, fails test_contract_misnamed_heading_fails. I planted 19 more, each failing at least one test:
  - heading order;
  - empty section;
  - missing heading;
  - repeated heading;
  - fenced code;
  - each of the three line comparisons;
  - the §0.5 list;
  - the thousands separator;
  - the case-insensitive lookup, in the check and in the rewrite;
  - all-or-nothing writing;
  - the section 1 bounds;
  - CRLF;
  - the xtask exception;
  - `###` subsections.
  All 20 were killed, and the file was restored and checked by sha256.
- Trial of --write-budget on the 17 real contracts, in a throwaway clone at 96688ca (fmine-runtime is now the 17th):
  - all 17 changed, with 48 lines replaced and none outside the three keys;
  - a second run was byte-identical;
  - the census went from 268 errors to 205. Every remaining error is a heading or section error, except xtask's hand-written Subsystem value `` `Testpit` `` (with backticks), which has no registry row to write from.
  So S2 is content work plus that one line.
- Gates at 96688ca:
  - clippy -D warnings: exit 0;
  - cargo test --workspace: 1074 passed, 0 failed, 43 ignored;
  - check-all: exit 0;
  - cargo fmt --check: exit 1, only on crates/fmine-cli/src/guidance_capacity.rs, which came in with 9bb92fc, not with this change;
